WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.275
Here's the two cell wing box.

00:00:02.275 --> 00:00:09.620
The torque is counterclockwise, but the problem doesn't give its size, so we'll find each shear flow per unit of torque.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.763
Notice the boom areas in the table.

00:00:12.763 --> 00:00:16.000
In pure torsion they don't matter at all.

00:00:17.533 --> 00:00:21.097
Take the reference G as twenty seven thousand six hundred.

00:00:21.097 --> 00:00:22.941
The webs keep their thickness.

00:00:22.941 --> 00:00:28.533
The skins, at twenty four thousand two hundred, are scaled by zero point eight seven seven.

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:33.567
Now delta for each wall is its length over t star.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.646
Around cell one: one nineteen sixty nine.

00:00:37.646 --> 00:00:40.253
Around cell two: thirty five twenty eight.

00:00:40.253 --> 00:00:43.420
The shared spar alone: one ninety nine point eight.

00:00:44.333 --> 00:00:59.053
Equal twist: q one times nineteen sixty nine, minus q two times one ninety nine point eight, over two times two thirty two thousand, equals the same for cell two.

00:00:59.466 --> 00:01:02.335
Cross multiply and collect.

00:01:02.335 --> 00:01:11.365
That leaves five fifty four million q one equals eight hundred seventy million q two.

00:01:11.365 --> 00:01:16.146
So q one is one point five seven times q two.

00:01:16.633 --> 00:01:18.784
Now the torque equation.

00:01:18.784 --> 00:01:27.386
T equals two times two thirty two thousand q one, plus two times two fifty eight thousand q two.

00:01:27.386 --> 00:01:32.673
Substituting, that's one point two four four million q two.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:39.980
So q two is zero point eight zero four times ten to the minus six, T.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:46.460
And q one is one point two six one times ten to the minus six, T.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:58.940
For a torque of one kilonewton meter: one point two six in cell one, zero point eight zero in cell two, and the spar carries the difference, zero point four six newtons per millimeter.

00:01:59.366 --> 00:02:00.184
Your turn.

00:02:00.184 --> 00:02:06.646
Pause here and do checkpoint five point one: a two cell box with a real torque.

00:02:10.499 --> 00:02:11.504
Let's recap.

00:02:11.504 --> 00:02:14.017
Booms carry the direct stress.

00:02:14.017 --> 00:02:24.819
The skin carries shear, and any direct stress it takes is added to the booms with t D b over six times two plus the stress ratio.

00:02:25.832 --> 00:02:33.337
The shear flow is constant between booms, and jumps by minus S y over I x x, B r y r, at each one.

00:02:33.337 --> 00:02:37.472
Closed sections: cut, march, then close with q s zero.

00:02:37.799 --> 00:02:41.588
In pure torsion, each cell has one shear flow.

00:02:41.588 --> 00:02:46.693
The torque gives one equation, and equal twist gives the rest.

00:02:46.693 --> 00:02:50.399
Different materials just scale the thickness.
